1. Introduction to the Tutorial
Welcome, future programmer! Today, you are going to build a "Nail Polish Matcher" program from scratch. This program helps users pick a color or find a polish that matches their skin tone based on a logical set of rules.
To keep things simple and clear, we will follow three strict rules:
The Basics Only: We will use only the simplest building blocks of Python. No complex functions or advanced libraries are allowed!
Line-by-Line Learning: We will present the code first, explain the logic in plain English, and then test your knowledge.
Knowledge Checks: Every phase concludes with a 3-question quiz. Make sure you understand each part before moving to the next!
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Phase 1: Starting the Program and Welcoming the User
Every good program starts by greeting the user and letting them know what is happening.
The Code
print("Welcome to the Nail Polish Matcher!")
Teaching Component
The print() function is the most basic way to communicate. It takes whatever is inside the parentheses and displays it on the screen. In Python, text is called a string. To tell Python that something is a string (and not a command), you must wrap the text in quotation marks (like "this"). Think of print() as the program’s "voice."
