3. Phase 2: Creating the Main Menu Loop
We want our program to stay open so the user can try different options without having to restart the script manually.
The Code
while True:
Teaching Component
A loop is a way to repeat actions. The command while True: creates an "infinite loop." Because the condition is set to "True," the program will keep repeating every line of code indented underneath it forever, until we specifically tell it to break (which we will learn later).
Quiz Component
