a) To run a section of code once.
b) To repeat a section of code multiple times.
c) To check for spelling errors.
What does True signify in while True:?
a) The loop should run as long as the condition remains true (which is forever here).
b) The user has typed the correct password.
c) The program is finished.
How does Python know which code is "inside" the loop?
a) The code is highlighted in blue.
b) The code is indented (moved to the right with spaces).
c) The code is written in all capital letters.
