4. Phase 3: Displaying Menu Options and Capturing Input
Now the program needs to give the user choices and listen for their answer.
The Code
    print("1. Pick a color.")
    print("2. Match skin tone.")
    selection = input("Please enter your choice (1 or 2): ")
Teaching Component
The input() function allows the user to "talk" back to the program. It pauses the program and waits for the user to type something. When they hit Enter, that answer is stored in a variable. A variable is like a labeled container; here, our container is named selection.
Important Note: The input() function always treats what the user types as text (a string), even if they type a number. This is why we will look for "1" later instead of just 1.
