5. Phase 4: Logic for Option 1 (Color Selection)
If the user picks the first option, the program needs to react to that specific choice.
The Code
    if selection == "1":
        color = input("What is your preferred color? ")
        print("You have selected " + color + ".")
Teaching Component
An if statement is a "fork in the road." It tells the program: "Only run the indented code IF this specific condition is true." We use == (double equals) to check if the value inside selection is exactly the same as the string "1". Note the quotes around the 1—remember, input() always gives us a string!
Quiz Component
