a) Because input() data is stored as a string, so we must compare it to a string.
b) To make the code look more professional.
c) To make the number 1 bigger.
What happens if the if condition is NOT met (e.g., the user types "3")?
a) The program crashes.
b) The program skips the indented code under the if statement.
c) The program deletes the selection variable.
