6. Phase 5: Logic for Option 2 (Skin Tone Matching)
If the user didn't pick "1", we need to check if they picked "2".
The Code
    elif selection == "2":
        tone = input("Enter your skin tone (Warm, Cool, or Neutral). Type 'Unknown' if you are unsure: ")
Teaching Component
The elif command stands for "else if." It allows the program to check a second condition only if the first if statement was false. We use it here to handle the user selecting "2". We then ask the user for their skin tone and give them specific options to choose from.
